A *T result (pointer to a bare type parameter) matches every pointer demand and, through
the value/pointer bridge, every value demand: the same universal-producer footgun as a
bare T result. It is rejected symmetrically, before it can silently capture unrelated
demands like *int here.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrBareTypeParamResult
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Thing struct{}

//plumb:build
func Default[T any]() *T { return new(T) }

//plumb:build
func NewThing(p *int) *Thing { return &Thing{} }
